      "content": "Is it possible that the uneven temperature rise is localized? I'm worried about some specific spots on the rotor getting way hotter than the rest, causing these sudden, almost mischievous shifts in braking force. Does the material breakdown happen globally, or are we looking at localized pockets of failure?",
